---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { resumeProfile } from "../lib/resume";

const emailHref = `mailto:${resumeProfile.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Platform / PCI Linux")}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Eirik Breen, senior systems consultant in Oslo. PCI DSS Linux, Kubernetes with GitOps, and network HSMs at Orange Business."
>
  <article class="page about-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">I run Linux platforms that have to pass an audit.</h1>
      <p class="page-meta">senior systems consultant · orange business (basefarm) · oslo</p>
      <p class="page-lede">
        I design and run Kubernetes for customers at Orange Business. The PCI DSS Linux environments I run have
        made it through their security audits. I also lead a project for redundant network HSMs across data
        centres.
      </p>
    </header>

    <dl class="glance" aria-label="At a glance">
      <div>
        <dt>role</dt>
        <dd>Senior Systems Consultant, Service Delivery, since 2023</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>platform</dt>
        <dd>RHEL, K3s and MKS, Argo CD, Cilium, OpenBao and Vault</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>compliance</dt>
        <dd>PCI DSS environments, Thales network HSMs</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>automation</dt>
        <dd>Ansible, CI/CD pipelines</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>logging</dt>
        <dd>Splunk, Elastic Stack</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>based</dt>
        <dd>Oslo, Norway</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <section class="prose" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="work-heading">The work</h2>
      <p>
        The clusters are K3s and MKS on RHEL. GitOps goes through Argo CD. Cilium handles networking, and secrets
        live in OpenBao and Vault. Ansible and CI/CD do the routine changes. When I need to know what actually
        happened, I am in Splunk or Elastic.
      </p>
      <p>
        A lot of it runs under PCI DSS, so "probably fine" is not a deployment strategy. On the HSM side I have worked
        with both Thales PayShield and Luna; the project I lead is a redundant network HSM setup across data centres.
        I write the change so
        the person on the next shift can follow it. I will take a dull pipeline over automation that hides what it did.
      </p>
      <p>
        I came up through operations. Senior on the incident team at Orange Business before consulting, mostly RHEL
        and Azure, nights and weekends on the roster. I mentored apprentices through their trade exam. Before that,
        first and second line at HDO in Gjøvik, supporting AMK centres, out-of-hours clinics, and A&amp;E on Norway's
        emergency network. Trade certificate with distinction. I am glad I did that work. I am not trying to get back
        on the incident roster.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/resume">Read the CV for dates and the full stack</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose" aria-labelledby="after-heading">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="after-heading">After hours</h2>
      <p>
        The homelab is K3s. Claude Code and OpenCode started after hours and now show up in the day job. If a project
        lasts more than a weekend it lands with <a href="/projects">the other things I made</a> or
        <a href="/blog">on the blog</a>. The newest is <a href="/projects#baton">Baton</a>, an inbox and voice remote
        for coding agents on macOS, out soon. Before that came ModelTable, a live LLM price table on one Cloudflare
        Worker, and PixelWitness, a browser extension that scores images for likely AI generation without sending
        them off the machine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="contact prose" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="contact-heading">Write me</h2>
      <p>Platform work, PCI Linux, GitOps, or network HSMs. Email me.</p>
      <p class="cta">
        <a href={emailHref}>{resumeProfile.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="secondary">
        Dates, employers, and the full stack are on <a href="/resume">the CV</a>.
        <a href={resumeProfile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a> works if you prefer.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: min(100%, 40rem);
  }

  .about-page .page-title {
    max-width: 17ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5.6vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
  }

  .glance {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .glance div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.7rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .glance dt {
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .glance dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .contact {
    padding-top: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .cta {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.25rem !important;
  }

  .cta a {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.2vw, 1.85rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .secondary {
    color: var(--muted) !important;
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .glance div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
